      "summary": "Name: Scalable E-Commerce Microservices Platform Technology Stack: Language: Node.js (Express/NestJS), Python (FastAPI/Django) Database: PostgreSQL, MongoDB (per microservice) Messaging: Kafka/RabbitMQ for async communi\u2026",
      "wordCount": 553,
      "content": "### **Project Plan & Spec Sheet**\n\n---\n\n#### **1. Project Overview**\n**Name:** Scalable E-Commerce Microservices Platform\n**Technology Stack:**\n- **Language:** Node.js (Express/NestJS), Python (FastAPI/Django)\n- **Database:** PostgreSQL, MongoDB (per microservice)\n- **Messaging:** Kafka/RabbitMQ for async communication between services\n- **Containerization & Orchestration:** Docker + Kubernetes (or Docker Swarm)\n- **Service Mesh:** Istio/Linkerd for advanced service-to-service communication\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Microservices Specifications**\n| Service               | Responsibilities                                                                                     |\n|-----------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **User Service**      | User authentication, profile management, role-based access control (JWT/OAuth).                      |\n| **Product Catalog**   | CRUD operations for products, inventory tracking, category management.                               |\n| **Shopping Cart**     | Persistent cart storage (Redis), item addition/removal/update quantities.                            |\n| **Order Service**      | Order placement, status updates (pending/paid/shipped/cancelled).                                  |\n| **Payment Service**   | Integration with Stripe/PayPal for transaction processing & refunds.                               |\n| **Notification Service** | Email/SMS alerts via Twilio/SendGrid for order confirmations, shipping updates.                     |\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Docker Compose Setup**\n```yaml\nversion: '3.8'\n\nservices:\n  # Databases (PostgreSQL + MongoDB)\n  postgres:\n    image: postgres:15-alpine\n    environment:\n      POSTGRES_USER: user\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: password\n      POSTGRES_DB: ecommerce_db\n\n  mongodb:\n    image: mongo:6.0\n    ports:\n      - \"27018:27017\"\n\n  # Redis for caching & session storage (Shopping Cart)\n  redis:\n    image: redis:7-alpine\n    ports:\n      - \"6379:6379\"\n\n  # Kafka/RabbitMQ for async messaging\n  kafka:\n    image: bitnami/kafka:2.8\n    environment:\n      KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS: PLAINTEXT://localhost:19092\n\n  # API Gateway (Traefik/Nginx)\n  api-gateway:\n    build: ./api-gateway\n    ports:\n      - \"3000:80\"\n    depends_on:\n      - user-service\n      - product-catalog\n      - order-service\n\n  # Microservices\n  user-service:\n    build: ./user-service\n    environment:\n      DB_URL: postgres://user:password@postgres/ecommerce_db?schema=public\n      JWT_SECRET: \"secret_key\"\n    depends_on:\n      - postgres\n\n  product-catalog:\n    build: ./product-catalog\n    environment:\n      MONGO_URI: mongodb://mongo:ecommerce_db\n    depends_on:\n      - mongodb\n\n  shopping-cart:\n    build: ./shopping-cart\n    environment:\n      REDIS_URL: redis://redis:6379/1\n    ports:\n      - \"5002:80\"\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **4. Starter Prompt for LLM Agentic Coding**\n**Task:** Implement the following microservices using Node.js (Express/NestJS) and Docker.\n\n### **User Service (`user-service`)**\n- **Features:**\n  - User registration/login with JWT authentication.\n  - Profile management (update, delete).\n  - Role-based access control (Admin/User).\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Express route for user login\napp.post('/login', async (req, res) => {\n    const { email, password } = req.body;\n    // Validate credentials & issue JWT token\n});\n```\n\n### **Product Catalog (`product-catalog`)**\n- **Features:**\n  - CRUD operations on products.\n  - Inventory management with stock checks.\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Add a product to MongoDB\nconst addProduct = async (req, res) => {\n    const { name, price, description } = req.body;\n    // Insert into MongoDB & return success response\n};\n```\n\n### **Shopping Cart (`shopping-cart`)**\n- **Features:**\n  - Persistent cart storage via Redis.\n  - Add/remove items with quantity updates.\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Add item to cart (Redis)\nconst addToCart = async (userId, productId) => {\n    // Increment stock in Product Catalog service first?\n};\n```\n\n### **Order Service (`order-service`)**\n- **Features:**\n  - Order placement via REST API.\n  - Status updates (pending/paid/shipped).\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Create order & trigger Payment Service\nconst createOrder = async ({ userId, items }) => {\n    // Save to DB + emit Kafka event for payment processing\n};\n```\n\n### **API Gateway (`api-gateway`)**\n- **Features:**\n  - Route requests to appropriate microservices.\n  - Load balancing (e.g., using Traefik).\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Express route in API Gateway\napp.use('/users', userServiceRouter);\napp.use('/products', productCatalogRouter);\n```\n\n### **Docker Compose Deployment**\n- Run `docker-compose up --build` to deploy all services.\n- Use Kubernetes for scaling (e.g., horizontal pod autoscaling).\n\n---\n**Next Steps:**\n1. Set up Dockerfiles for each microservice with Node.js/Python dependencies.\n2. Implement REST/GraphQL APIs in NestJS/FastAPI.\n3. Add Kafka/RabbitMQ integration for async communication between services.\n\nWould you like to proceed with a specific service first?"
