      "content": "# Static Markdown Site Generator with UV\n\nI want to create a Python project using `uv` that converts a folder of markdown files into a static HTML website.\n\n## Project Requirements:\n- **Project name:** `md-site-gen` (or similar)\n- **Create it in a new folder** with complete project structure\n- **Use `uv`** for package management with `pyproject.toml`\n- **Convert markdown to HTML** with styled output\n- **Generate an index page** listing all converted files\n- **Use Jinja2 templates** for HTML generation\n\n## Features to Include:\n1. Scan a `docs/` or `content/` folder for all `.md` files\n2. Convert each markdown file to HTML\n3. Generate an `index.html` page with links to all pages\n4. Create a simple CSS stylesheet for styling\n5. Output all HTML files to an `output/` or `build/` folder\n6. Bonus: Watch mode to auto-regenerate when files change\n\n## Tech Stack:\n- `python` (3.9+)\n- `markdown` (for MD to HTML conversion)\n- `jinja2` (for HTML templating)\n- `watchdog` (optional, for file watching)\n\n## Deliverables:\n- Complete project folder structure\n- `pyproject.toml` with all dependencies\n- Working Python script that converts my markdown files\n- Basic HTML and CSS templates\n- Clear instructions on how to run it with `uv`\n\nPlease scaffold the entire project ready to use!"
